# What goes in the SDIST — deliberately NOT the wheel.
#
# The wheel is code only: `tests/test_packaging_contents.py` asserts it contains zero
# non-.py entries outside dist-info. MANIFEST.in cannot add files to a wheel
# built by setuptools without `include_package_data`, which is exactly why it is the right
# tool here — it makes the source distribution complete (a contributor can `pip download
# --no-binary` and get a runnable checkout with the suites and the test suite) while
# leaving the installed program untouched.
graft examples
graft docs
graft tests
# MP-100: `graft tests` without this shipped a suite that cannot import itself -- [M] an
# unpacked sdist collected 2 errors, `No module named 'scripts'`, because
# tests/test_recall_arm.py and tests/test_fp_measurement_repertoire.py do
# `from scripts.fp_measurement import ...`. It is not only the tests: the Drift Map's own
# published reproduce command is `python scripts/drift_map.py`, and README links
# scripts/fp_measurement.py. Enforced by test_packaging_contents.py, which now runs
# `pytest --collect-only` INSIDE the unpacked sdist -- a name list cannot see this.
graft scripts
include data/models.json
include CONTRIBUTING.md CHANGELOG.md SECURITY.md CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
include action.yml
prune ops
prune .claude
prune reports
global-exclude *.pyc __pycache__/*
